# Smart Rename (iurysza/herdr-tab-smart-rename), installed by run_after_53.
#
# The plugin names tabs from deterministic process rules first, and only asks a
# model when those rules find the work ambiguous. That model is reached through
# OpenRouter, which speaks the OpenAI-compatible protocol the plugin needs
# (@ai-sdk/openai-compatible). Any provider name other than openai or kimi-code
# reads its key from SMART_RENAME_API_KEY.
#
# The key is its own KeePass entry, separate from the Hermes OpenRouter key, so
# either can be revoked alone.
#
# Model: openai/gpt-5.6-luna, the small tier of the plugin's default family,
# chosen as capable enough to name a tab while costing $0.20 in / $1.20 out per
# million tokens on OpenRouter (2026-10-02).
SMART_RENAME_PROVIDER=openrouter
SMART_RENAME_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
SMART_RENAME_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.6-luna
SMART_RENAME_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
SMART_RENAME_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
SMART_RENAME_API_KEY={{ (keepassxc "OpenRouter :: API Key (herdr-tab-smart-rename)").Password }}

# Optional custom naming prompt; a relative path resolves from this directory.
# The default prompt is the plugin's own docs/naming-policy.md.
# SMART_RENAME_PROMPT_PATH=naming-prompt.md
